# Source wavs of the end-to-end Python<->C parity gate (make test-parity-e2e).
# python/diag/gen_aec_e2e_golden.py reads exactly this pair (CASE = 0I0XMl3M0ECO0U1N0cJvpg_doubletalk,
# native 16 kHz; the 8 kHz / 48 kHz goldens are scipy resample_poly derivatives of the SAME pair).
# wav/aec_challenge_blind/ is git-ignored (local dataset), so this pin is the only integrity link
# between a checkout and the goldens the gate regenerates from it.
# Format = `shasum -a 256 -c` format; paths are relative to <aec>/wav (run `cd wav && shasum -a 256 -c
# ../c_impl/test/parity_e2e_inputs.sha256`). A missing file or a hash mismatch fails the gate.
